From 6b0445bd0b60186b9d5bef78bc87d7cc6cfc9df8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Adhemerval Zanella <adhemerval.zanella@linaro.org>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 14:28:33 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] Makefile.in: Run the build directory goals serially (BZ
 34699)

The builddir Makefile runs a separate make in the source directory
for each goal, so 'make -jN check xcheck' runs both at the same time.

Since a subdirectory's xtests also builds and runs its tests, the two
instances build the same targets concurrently and fail when renaming
the shared temporary files.

Add .NOTPARALLEL so the goals run one after another; each still builds
in parallel.

Checked on x86_64-linux-gnu.

Reviewed-by: Arjun Shankar <arjun@redhat.com>

(cherry picked from commit 83daf36f1251d17200ffe7cce56e21f632a0c98e)
[LibreELEC Hades: the NEWS hunk of this commit is left out. NEWS is not
built, and the NEWS of this series differs from the branch.]
---
 Makefile.in | 2 ++
 2 files changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Makefile.in b/Makefile.in
index e40dcbb..9fd5468 100644
--- a/Makefile.in
+++ b/Makefile.in
@@ -16,6 +16,8 @@ test-supported-fortify = @libc_cv_test_supported_fortify_source@
 
 .PHONY: all install bench
 
+.NOTPARALLEL:
+
 all .DEFAULT:
 	$(MAKE) -r PARALLELMFLAGS="$(PARALLELMFLAGS)" -C $(srcdir) objdir=`pwd` $@
 